snp1.7:27.1 starts: Mounting the divine chariot,
snp1.7:27.2 starts: and the great, stainless road,
snp1.7:27.3 starts: dispassioned for sensual passion,
snp1.7:27.4 starts: he reached the world of the Brahmās.
snp1.7:27.5 starts: His birth didn’t prevent him
snp1.7:27.6 starts: from reaching the world of the Brahmās.
snp1.8:7.1 starts: As a mother would risk her life
snp1.8:7.2 starts: to protect her child, her only child,
snp1.8:7.3 starts: even so should one cultivate the heart limitlessly
snp1.8:7.4 starts: with regard to all beings.
snp1.9:13.1 starts: Consummate the mind of the sage
snp1.9:13.2 starts: in action & in ways of speech,
snp1.9:13.3 starts: you rightly rejoice in him
snp1.9:13.4 starts: as consummate in clear-knowing & conduct.
snp1.9:14.1 starts: Consummate the mind of the sage
snp1.9:14.2 starts: in action & in ways of speech,
snp1.9:14.3 starts: let’s go see Gotama,
snp1.9:14.4 starts: consummate in clear-knowing & conduct.
snp1.7:23.1 starts: Whoever, though not an arahant,
snp1.7:23.2 starts: claims to be an arahant:
snp1.7:23.3 starts: He is the thief in this world
snp1.7:23.4 starts: He is the vilest of outcastes.
snp1.7:23.5 starts: These are said to be outcastes,
snp1.7:23.6 starts: as I have proclaimed them to you.
snp1.7:26.1 starts: He, Mātaṅga,
snp1.7:26.2 starts: hard to gain.
snp1.7:26.3 starts: They came into his service,
snp1.7:26.4 starts: many noble warriors & brahmans.
snp1.9:12.1 starts: Hemavata the yakkha:
snp1.9:12.2 starts: in action & in ways of speech,
snp1.9:12.3 starts: you rightly praise him
snp1.9:12.4 starts: as consummate in clear-knowing & conduct.
snp1.9:15.1 starts: Come, let’s go see Gotama,
snp1.9:15.2 starts: with legs like an antelope, thin,
snp1.9:15.3 starts: eating little, not greedy,
snp1.9:15.4 starts: doing jhāna in the forest.
snp1.9:17.1 starts: Let’s ask Gotama,
snp1.9:17.2 starts: attained to the far shore
snp1.9:17.3 starts: awakened,
snp1.9:17.4 starts: gone past animosity
snp1.10:10.1 starts: Āḷavaka:
snp1.10:10.2 starts: How does one find wealth?
snp1.10:10.3 starts: How does one attain honor?
snp1.10:10.4 starts: How bind friends to oneself?
snp1.10:10.5 starts: Passing from this world
snp1.10:10.6 starts: how does one not grieve?
snp1.10:11.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp1.10:11.2 starts: for attaining unbinding,
snp1.10:11.3 starts: one listening well
snp1.10:11.4 starts: gains discernment.
snp1.10:13.1 starts: Endowed with these four qualities,
snp1.10:13.2 starts: —truth,
snp1.10:13.3 starts: a householder of conviction,
snp1.10:13.4 starts: on passing away, doesn’t grieve.
